:"sec/raw/4c86076baf159e12f80912bd0b7ee6696495b8356758036a622646ce12378d42.bin","sha256":"4c86076baf159e12f80912bd0b7ee6696495b8356758036a622646ce12378d42"}},{"id":"1b30c714619a41e215ba8059fcb38dccdb41abc16ff83c0a56a63242571da917","quote":"Cost of revenue increased by $68 thousand, or 111%, for the three months ended June 30, 2026 as compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. The increase was primarily due to materials costs related to our DARPA program.","context":"Cost of Revenue","section":"The following table sets forth our results of operations for the periods indicated:","block":674,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0002097163-26-000020","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0002097163","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2097163/000209716326000020/xndu-20260630_d2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/4c86076baf159e12f80912bd0b7ee6696495b8356758036a622646ce12378d42.bin","sha256":"4c86076baf159e12f80912bd0b7ee6696495b8356758036a622646ce12378d42"}},{"id":"332f2b0b45c4b71f266823689f31fbc7ccf09d9e3a3ec6a5be659aa540f25af8","quote":"As a percentage of total revenue, cost of revenue was 8% and 6% for the three months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, respectively. These costs remain low as the revenue contracts the Company enters into are aligned with our underlying R&D roadmap and only incremental costs to complete the performance obligations are included in cost of revenue.","context":"Cost of revenue increased by $68 thousand, or 111%, for the three months ended June 30, 2026 as compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. The increase was primarily due to materials costs related to our DARPA program.","section":"The following table sets forth our results of operations for the periods indicated:","block":675,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0002097163-26-000020","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0002097163","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2097163/000209716326000020/xndu-20260630_d2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/4c86076baf159e12f80912bd0b7ee6696495b8356758036a622646ce12378d42.bin","sha256":"4c86076baf159e12f80912bd0b7ee6696495b8356758036a622646ce12378d42"}},{"id":"ca2b09f4a1da3a524ad3615887ccae8948d4d847cb9241d2ee98627b196bd03b","quote":"Research and development expenses increased by $6.7 million, or 52%, for the three months ended June 30, 2026 as compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. The increase was primarily driven by higher payroll-related expenses, including stock-based compensation, compared to the prior period. The higher payroll-related expenses were primarily due to increased headcount, which increased 24% period-over-period, and restricted share unit (\"RSU\") grants awarded in the second quarter of 2026. Higher material consumption also contributed to the increase.","context":"Research and Development","section":"MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":680,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0002097163-26-000020","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0002097163","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2097163/000209716326000020/xndu-20260630_d2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/4c86076baf159e12f80912bd0b7ee6696495b8356758036a622646ce12378d42.bin","sha256":"4c86076baf159e12f80912bd0b7ee6696495b8356758036a622646ce12378d42"}},{"id":"425b4741687fa9788c8fe4ec116fccf7e081c3d3ec8b9689a5a294522e5e869d","quote":"General and administrative expenses increased by $8.9 million, or 406%, for the three months ended June 30, 2026 as compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. The increase was primarily driven by higher professional fees, including audit, regulatory, legal and capital markets fees associated with the SATM and operations as a public company, as well as an advisory fee related to the Reverse Recapitalization. The increase was also driven by higher payroll-related costs, including stock-based compensation, resulting from RSUs granted during the quarter and a 63% increase in general and administrative headcount compared to the prior-year period.","context":"General and Administrative","section":"MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":682,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0002097163-26-000020","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0002097163","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2097163/000209716326000020/xndu-20260630_d2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/4c86076baf159e12f80912bd0b7ee6696495b8356758036a622646ce12378d42.bin","sha256":"4c86076baf159e12f80912bd0b7ee6696495b8356758036a622646ce12378d42"}},{"id":"8267c045fab6ebc8966e6ff9e5af7acd0ab0295b4da921ca0c1716c9a5f8281b","quote":"Sales and marketing expenses increased by $175 thousand, or 47%, for the three months ended June 30, 2026 as compared to the three months ended June 30, 2025. The increase was primarily due to higher public relations and marketing related costs to help support our growth as a newly publicly listed company as well as increased payroll-related costs, including stock based compensation.","context":"Sales and Marketing","section":"MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":684,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0002097163-26-000020","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0002097163","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2097163/000209716326000020/xndu-20260630_d2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/4c86076baf159e12f80912bd0b7e